     "id": "notes-1",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Purpose.** See equilibrium as the output at which nobody is surprised: where planned spending equals production and unplanned inventory investment is zero. Then see the multiplier as the horizontal jump in the crossing when the PE line shifts up.\n- **Model.** A view of [Keynesian Cross Expenditure Model](note:keynesian-cross-expenditure-model).\n- **Elements.** Panel `cross`: curves `line45`, `pe`; points `eq`, `produce` (draggable, bound to `Yp`), `spend`; line `gap`. Readouts `Ystar_out`, `Iu_out`, `mult_out`.\n- **Goal it supports.** `abs(Iu) < 1`: met only at $Y = 1{,}100$ on the step-10 grid.\n- **Tests.** Python, closed form."
      }
     ],
     "words": 92,
     "symbols": [
      "$Y$"
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
